  "description": "KEYQAJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H78 Eu4 N8 O38 Zn4,2(C1 H4 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1A (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.378-3.903 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.45-125.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd4Zn8L8(OAc)8](OH)4 (crystallographic formula C208H267N16O68Zn8Nd4). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
